From 15db6f979b0d895eb937e82e040a078c87798131 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:36:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/69] CUDA/HIP: MMVQ pair launch for two products of the same
 src1 (GGML_HIP_MMVQ_PAIR)

Two consecutive MUL_MATs with the same weight type and K on the same src1 (2-8 columns) run as one multi-column
MMVQ grid: the blocks past the first matrix compute the second one (pair_x/pair_dst/pair_nrows in the fusion args,
bias_only instantiation). Same per-block code, reduction order and q8_1 activations as two launches, so bitwise
equal; no extra registers (unlike the gate+up accumulator fusion, -8%). Skipped when the second product has its own
bias/scale epilogue. qwen35 expands the GDN qkv and z products next to each other so they can pair.
GGML_HIP_MMVQ_PAIR=0 restores two launches. test-backend-ops: MUL_MAT_PAIR (equal and different row counts).

Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL (pairs: ffn up/gate 40, GDN qkv/z 22 of 64/48 layers), rocprofv3 in the server, MTP n=4
(measured together with the next two commits): verify graph 972 -> 911 kernels, MMVQ 21.96 -> 21.67 ms per verify.
Greedy md5 (plain and MTP) equal to 9f83f1f81. test-backend-ops MUL_MAT_PAIR 98/98, MUL_MAT_ADD 360/360,
MUL_MAT 2444/2444 (one flaky q5_0 n=1 NMSE miss in ~10 runs, unrelated path).
